          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>What is the value of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\dfrac 1 6 \\div 5 ?]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "What is the value of [MATH: \\dfrac 1 6 \\div 5 ?]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Dividing a fraction by a whole number is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of that whole number.</p><p>The reciprocal of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\color{blue}5]</span> is <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\dfrac{1}{{\\color{blue}{5}}}.]</span> So, we have</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\dfrac 1 6\\, {\\color{red}\\div} \\, {\\color{blue}5} = \\dfrac 1 6\\, {\\color{red}\\times} \\,\\dfrac{1}{\\color{blue}5}.]</span> </p><p>Now, we multiply the fractions. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\dfrac 1 6 \\times \\dfrac{1}{5} = \\dfrac {1\\times 1} {6\\times 5} = \\dfrac{1}{30}]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Dividing a fraction by a whole number is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of that whole number.\n\nThe reciprocal of [MATH: \\color{blue}5] is [MATH: \\dfrac{1}{{\\color{blue}{5}}}.] So, we have\n\n[MATH: \\dfrac 1 6\\, {\\color{red}\\div} \\, {\\color{blue}5} = \\dfrac 1 6\\, {\\color{red}\\times} \\,\\dfrac{1}{\\color{blue}5}.]\n\nNow, we multiply the fractions. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n[MATH: \\dfrac 1 6 \\times \\dfrac{1}{5} = \\dfrac {1\\times 1} {6\\times 5} = \\dfrac{1}{30}]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nWhat is the value of [MATH: \\dfrac 1 6 \\div 5 ?]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nDividing a fraction by a whole number is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of that whole number.\n\nThe reciprocal of [MATH: \\color{blue}5] is [MATH: \\dfrac{1}{{\\color{blue}{5}}}.] So, we have\n\n[MATH: \\dfrac 1 6\\, {\\color{red}\\div} \\, {\\color{blue}5} = \\dfrac 1 6\\, {\\color{red}\\times} \\,\\dfrac{1}{\\color{blue}5}.]\n\nNow, we multiply the fractions. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n[MATH: \\dfrac 1 6 \\times \\dfrac{1}{5} = \\dfrac {1\\times 1} {6\\times 5} = \\dfrac{1}{30}]"
      },
