        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Find the value of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\dfrac{6}{11} \\div 3 .]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Find the value of [MATH: \\dfrac{6}{11} \\div 3 .]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Dividing a fraction by a whole number is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of that whole number.</p><p>The reciprocal of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\color{blue}3]</span> is <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\dfrac{1}{{\\color{blue}{3}}}.]</span> So, we have</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\dfrac {6}{11} \\, {\\color{red}\\div} \\, {\\color{blue}3} =  \\dfrac {6}{11}\\, {\\color{red}\\times} \\,\\dfrac{1}{\\color{blue}3}.]</span> </p><p>Now, we multiply fractions. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\dfrac {6}{11} \\times \\dfrac{1}{3} = \\dfrac {6\\times 1} {11\\times 3} = \\dfrac{6}{33}]</span></p><p>Finally, we simplify our result by dividing the numerator and denominator by <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 3\\mathbin{:}]</span></p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\dfrac{6}{33} = \\dfrac{6\\div 3}{33\\div 3} = \\dfrac{2}{11}]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Dividing a fraction by a whole number is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of that whole number.\n\nThe reciprocal of [MATH: \\color{blue}3] is [MATH: \\dfrac{1}{{\\color{blue}{3}}}.] So, we have\n\n[MATH: \\dfrac {6}{11} \\, {\\color{red}\\div} \\, {\\color{blue}3} = \\dfrac {6}{11}\\, {\\color{red}\\times} \\,\\dfrac{1}{\\color{blue}3}.]\n\nNow, we multiply fractions. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n[MATH: \\dfrac {6}{11} \\times \\dfrac{1}{3} = \\dfrac {6\\times 1} {11\\times 3} = \\dfrac{6}{33}]\n\nFinally, we simplify our result by dividing the numerator and denominator by [MATH: 3\\mathbin{:}]\n\n[MATH: \\dfrac{6}{33} = \\dfrac{6\\div 3}{33\\div 3} = \\dfrac{2}{11}]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
