        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nFind the value of [MATH: \\dfrac{6}{11} \\div 3 .]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nDividing a fraction by a whole number is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of that whole number.\n\nThe reciprocal of [MATH: \\color{blue}3] is [MATH: \\dfrac{1}{{\\color{blue}{3}}}.] So, we have\n\n[MATH: \\dfrac {6}{11} \\, {\\color{red}\\div} \\, {\\color{blue}3} = \\dfrac {6}{11}\\, {\\color{red}\\times} \\,\\dfrac{1}{\\color{blue}3}.]\n\nNow, we multiply fractions. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n[MATH: \\dfrac {6}{11} \\times \\dfrac{1}{3} = \\dfrac {6\\times 1} {11\\times 3} = \\dfrac{6}{33}]\n\nFinally, we simplify our result by dividing the numerator and denominator by [MATH: 3\\mathbin{:}]\n\n[MATH: \\dfrac{6}{33} = \\dfrac{6\\div 3}{33\\div 3} = \\dfrac{2}{11}]"
