    "readable_text": "Item 1 \u2014 Tutorial: Introduction\n\nContent:\nTo divide a fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction by the whole number's reciprocal.\n\nContent:\nLet's use this rule to solve the following division problem:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \\dfrac14 \\div {\\color{blue}{3}}]\n\nContent:\nThe reciprocal of [MATH: \\color{blue}3] is [MATH: \\dfrac{1}{{\\color{blue}{3}}}.] So, we have\n[MATH: \\dfrac 1 4\\, {\\color{red}\\div} \\, {\\color{blue}3} = \\dfrac 1 4\\, {\\color{red}\\times} \\,\\dfrac{1}{\\color{blue}3}.]\n\nContent:\nNow, we multiply fractions. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n[MATH: \\dfrac 1 4 \\times \\dfrac{1}{3} = \\dfrac {1\\times 1} {4\\times 3} = \\dfrac{1}{12}]\n\nContent:\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \\dfrac14 \\div 3 = \\dfrac{1}{12}.]\n\nContent:\nWe get the same result by using a fraction model:\n\nGraphic:\n[IMG: /graphics/b3ae646b104ebb9f50e63ae6094834bb]\n\n---\n\nItem 2 \u2014 Example: Dividing a Unit Fraction by a Whole Number\n\nExample Prompt:\nWhat is the value of [MATH: \\dfrac 1 6 \\div 5 ?]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nDividing a fraction by a whole number is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of that whole number.\n\nThe reciprocal of [MATH: \\color{blue}5] is [MATH: \\dfrac{1}{{\\color{blue}{5}}}.] So, we have\n\n[MATH: \\dfrac 1 6\\, {\\color{red}\\div} \\, {\\color{blue}5} = \\dfrac 1 6\\, {\\color{red}\\times} \\,\\dfrac{1}{\\color{blue}5}.]\n\nNow, we multiply the fractions. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n[MATH: \\dfrac 1 6 \\times \\dfrac{1}{5} = \\dfrac {1\\times 1} {6\\times 5} = \\dfrac{1}{30}]\n\n---\n\nItem 3 \u2014 Question 1\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: (1)/(7) \u00f7 3 =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: (7)/(3)]\nb. [MATH: (3)/(7)]\nc. [MATH: (10)/(21)]\nd. [MATH: (1)/(21)]\ne. [MATH: (10)/(7)]\n\n---\n\nItem 4 \u2014 Question 2\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: (1)/(7) \u00f7 6 =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: (6)/(7)]\nb. [MATH: 40]\nc. [MATH: 42]\nd. [MATH: (1)/(42)]\ne. [MATH: (7)/(6)]\n\n---\n\nItem 5 \u2014 Example: Dividing a Fraction by a Whole Number\n\nExample Prompt:\nWhat is the values of [MATH: \\dfrac 2 3 \\div 7 ?]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nDividing a fraction by a whole number is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of that whole number.\n\nThe reciprocal of [MATH: \\color{blue}7] is [MATH: \\dfrac{1}{{\\color{blue}{7}}}.] So, we have\n\n[MATH: \\dfrac 2 3\\, {\\color{red}\\div} \\, {\\color{blue}7} = \\dfrac 2 3\\, {\\color{red}\\times} \\,\\dfrac{1}{\\color{blue}7} .]\n\nNow, we multiply fractions. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n[MATH: \\dfrac 2 3 \\times \\dfrac{1}{7} = \\dfrac {2\\times 1} {3\\times 7} = \\dfrac{2}{21}]\n\n---\n\nItem 6 \u2014 Question 3\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: (2)/(5) \u00f7 3 =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: (6)/(5)]\nb. [MATH: (1)/(5)]\nc. [MATH: (4)/(15)]\nd. [MATH: (2)/(15)]\ne. [MATH: (2)/(5)]\n\n---\n\nItem 7 \u2014 Question 4\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: (2)/(7) \u00f7 5 =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: (1)/(35)]\nb. [MATH: (2)/(25)]\nc. [MATH: (10)/(7)]\nd. [MATH: (15)/(7)]\ne. [MATH: (2)/(35)]\n\n---\n\nItem 8 \u2014 Example: Cases Where Simplification Is Required\n\nExample Prompt:\nFind the value of [MATH: \\dfrac{6}{11} \\div 3 .]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nDividing a fraction by a whole number is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of that whole number.\n\nThe reciprocal of [MATH: \\color{blue}3] is [MATH: \\dfrac{1}{{\\color{blue}{3}}}.] So, we have\n\n[MATH: \\dfrac {6}{11} \\, {\\color{red}\\div} \\, {\\color{blue}3} = \\dfrac {6}{11}\\, {\\color{red}\\times} \\,\\dfrac{1}{\\color{blue}3}.]\n\nNow, we multiply fractions. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n[MATH: \\dfrac {6}{11} \\times \\dfrac{1}{3} = \\dfrac {6\\times 1} {11\\times 3} = \\dfrac{6}{33}]\n\nFinally, we simplify our result by dividing the numerator and denominator by [MATH: 3\\mathbin{:}]\n\n[MATH: \\dfrac{6}{33} = \\dfrac{6\\div 3}{33\\div 3} = \\dfrac{2}{11}]\n\n---\n\nItem 9 \u2014 Question 5\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: (4)/(7) \u00f7 2 =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: (8)/(7)]\nb. [MATH: (2)/(7)]\nc. [MATH: (3)/(7)]\nd. [MATH: (6)/(7)]\ne. [MATH: (1)/(7)]\n\n---\n\nItem 10 \u2014 Question 6\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: (10)/(11) \u00f7 5 =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: (2)/(11)]\nb. [MATH: (50)/(11)]\nc. [MATH: (7)/(11)]\nd. [MATH: (9)/(55)]\ne. [MATH: (2)/(55)]"
